\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Audit coverage and prediction, measured. Missingness is below $0.6\%$ everywhere, so the unresolved tournaments come from requiring all ten scheduled judgments per edge rather than from parse failures. The order gap is the mean absolute difference between the two correctly oriented order-specific means, and at $0.53$--$0.69$ for IF, helpfulness and the joint control it is the size of the judge's position dependence: it is why no cyclic triangle survives both presentation orders. Truthfulness behaves differently, with $64.9\%$ ties and the smallest order gap, so it yields the fewest edges and the fewest triangles. On identical complete panel-B pairs the frozen GPM has the lower Brier loss on all four rubrics, by $.0016$ to $.0038$, but every paired prompt-bootstrap interval contains zero; the consistent sign across four rubrics is worth noting and is not a significant difference. Neither teacher was fitted or calibrated on the audit, and this predictive comparison establishes nothing about cycles.}}{24}{table.142}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:within-rubric-quality}{{10}{24}{Audit coverage and prediction, measured. Missingness is below $0.6\%$ everywhere, so the unresolved tournaments come from requiring all ten scheduled judgments per edge rather than from parse failures. The order gap is the mean absolute difference between the two correctly oriented order-specific means, and at $0.53$--$0.69$ for IF, helpfulness and the joint control it is the size of the judge's position dependence: it is why no cyclic triangle survives both presentation orders. Truthfulness behaves differently, with $64.9\%$ ties and the smallest order gap, so it yields the fewest edges and the fewest triangles. On identical complete panel-B pairs the frozen GPM has the lower Brier loss on all four rubrics, by $.0016$ to $.0038$, but every paired prompt-bootstrap interval contains zero; the consistent sign across four rubrics is worth noting and is not a significant difference. Neither teacher was fitted or calibrated on the audit, and this predictive comparison establishes nothing about cycles}{table.142}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Independent cycle confirmation, measured. No rubric yielded an eligible witness: the selection rule requires all three cycle directions to hold in each presentation order separately, and only $15$ of the $72$ cycle edges observed in panel A do, $20.8\%$. Every cyclic triangle A produced is therefore an artefact of order averaging rather than an order-robust cycle, consistent with the judge's strong first-position preference. No confirmation judgments were spent, and the protocol assigns $p=1$ where no witness is selected. ``Not confirmed'' does not mean transitive: it means this budget produced nothing to test.}}{24}{table.146}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:within-rubric-example}{{11}{24}{Independent cycle confirmation, measured. No rubric yielded an eligible witness: the selection rule requires all three cycle directions to hold in each presentation order separately, and only $15$ of the $72$ cycle edges observed in panel A do, $20.8\%$. Every cyclic triangle A produced is therefore an artefact of order averaging rather than an order-robust cycle, consistent with the judge's strong first-position preference. No confirmation judgments were spent, and the protocol assigns $p=1$ where no witness is selected. ``Not confirmed'' does not mean transitive: it means this budget produced nothing to test}{table.146}{}}
